---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { getPermalink } from '~/utils/permalinks';

const metadata = {
  title: 'About',
  description:
    'Abteen Arab’s personal research lab exploring computer vision, geometric understanding, world geometry modeling, and efficient and adaptive vision architectures.',
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <div class="lab-shell">
    <section class="lab-page-intro" aria-labelledby="about-title">
      <h1 id="about-title" class="lab-title max-w-4xl">About</h1>
      <div class="mt-7 max-w-2xl space-y-6">
        <p class="lab-lede">I'm Abteen Arab, and welcome to my personal lab.</p>
        <p class="lab-lede">
          My research interests lie broadly in computer vision, particularly in how visual representations interact with
          geometry, language, action, and other modalities. This space serves as a personal research wiki where I
          document ongoing projects, ideas, experiments, and directions that I find interesting.
        </p>
        <p class="lab-lede">
          I call it a personal lab because that is how I approach my independent research: as a collection of projects
          organized around a broader research theme rather than as isolated experiments. At the center of that theme is{
            ' '
          }
          <strong>geometric understanding</strong>—how models can build useful representations of the structure,
          dynamics, and eventually the physical behavior of the visual world.
        </p>
        <p class="lab-lede">
          My previous work has spanned 2D computer vision, 3D reconstruction, and visual geometry models. More recently,
          I have been exploring world geometry modeling, efficient and adaptive vision architectures, and ways of
          combining geometric representations with other forms of reasoning.
        </p>
        <p class="lab-lede">
          This site is where I share that work, along with unfinished ideas, technical notes, experiments, and research
          questions that I am actively thinking about.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="lab-rule lab-section" aria-label="Explore the work">
      <a class="lab-text-link" href={getPermalink('/research-highlights')}
        >Explore research highlights <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
      >
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
